build 19: a DARK look (the moon button by the logo, or the gear menu; each session remembers its own): the same drawing at night: near-black space, bone-white hairlines, a starfield with sparkles, a lit moon with a halo, the colonnade and the sea in white line art, the crystal glowing with a pool of light on the water, GENERATE glowing; the gem's luster is still the only colour. The LIGHT look is unchanged. Version 1.11.0. build 18: the screen redrawn in the spirit of Land of the Lustrous (Haruko Ichikawa's graphic style): paper-white negative space with a faint printed grain, ink-black hairlines and solid black blocks (the header, the chosen TAKE TYPE, the waveform strip, the keys' bed), and the gem's luster (mint, lilac, champagne, ice) as the only colour: on GENERATE (a cut gem), the chosen CHARACTER crystal, the TRIM part of the waveform, the lit keys. The picture is our own drawing in code: a colonnade receding to the horizon under one black lintel, the sea in hatched lines, the moon, and a tall cracked crystal at the water with shards lifting off and sparkles. Knobs are engraved dials, the slider thumb a small gem. Idle controls greyed out as before; fills any window shape. Version 1.10.0. build 17: the screen always fills the whole window, any size or shape (no empty space at the sides): the extra room goes to the picture, the TAKES box and the keys, the right-hand controls move with the edge; nothing stretches. Version 1.9.1. build 16: a brand-new screen, exactly Brandon's picture (the crystal valley: the anime landscape with the crystal, a deep navy frame, teal crystal accents, the engraved Cinzel letters). The old window is gone (the four looks, UNDER THE HOOD, TERRAIN, the STYLE browser, the CLEAR pill, VELOCITY, SCALE, the waveform's part boxes). TAKE TYPE rows, CHARACTER crystals, STYLE and LENGTH menus, the landscape takes a dropped sound anywhere, LOAD... / RECORD, the waveform strip with PLAY and TRIM (drag the part), NATURAL <-> MUSICAL, TONE / VOICE (DREAM, STUTTER, DRIFT by type) / SPACE, the crystal GENERATE, VARY, TAKES, PLAY | DRAG WAV | DRAG MIDI | DRAG CHORDS | SAVE TAKE, the keys C1 .. G7. Anything that does nothing right now is greyed out. CLEAR, the RECORD input, the key lock and TRIM reset are in the gear menu. Opens at 1140 x 760. The sound is untouched. Version 1.9.0. build 15: a TEMPO switch in the header, next to TEMPO: 1/2x | 1x | 2x, each showing the BPM it plays at. New takes are made at that tempo and the take on screen re-renders at it (the same idea); DRAG MIDI lands in FL exactly as you hear it (written at FL's tempo), DRAG WAV is the take as you hear it with the BPM in the file name; saved with the session, a new Ghost Slice starts at 1x. Version 1.8.2. build 14: opens at a size that fits FL Studio's plug-in window on a 1440 x 900 MacBook Pro (1054 x 760, the picture's own proportions; still resizable, and always this size when it opens), and a new Ghost Slice is always a fresh start (tested: two at once, the second stays at factory defaults). No other project's names in the window. Built and installed on Brandon's own Mac. Version 1.8.1. build 13: TERRAIN exactly like Brandon's reference (topographically.vercel.app): separate mountains of every kind (thin tall spires, flat-topped plateaus, little knolls) on one island, the land tilting up as the page opens, the chosen mountain lit with its outline, a height tag and a size tag (filled while you drag), height numbers riding in the rings, the TAG tool to write your own words on a ring, and the tiny three-button toolbar (our other buttons behind ...). The land now plays the whole take while you drag, not just its tone: spires STUTTER and SHIMMER, plateaus DREAM and hold, rough ground adds GRIT and backwards chops, merging mountains add SPACE, many mountains add CHORUS, the spread sets WIDTH, the land's lean sets TONE, a quick drag WOBBLEs; a small readout shows what the land is pushing, SHAPES picks a whole landscape (SPIRE FOREST, VOLCANO, PLATEAU, ARCHIPELAGO ...), and shuffle makes wild ones. Exports carry it. Takes with flat land, and every session saved before, sound exactly as they did. Version 1.8.0. build 12: TERRAIN. A new TERRAIN pill at the right end of the TAKES row opens a landscape over the whole window body: thin contour rings on a dark card, in your look's colours. Pull the ground up and a mountain rises; across is frequency (40 Hz to 16 kHz), back is later in the take, a mountain's height is resonance (up to +12 dB, a tall narrow one rings), its width is Q, a valley cuts, roughness adds grit. The take plays while you pull and you hear the landscape change live; let go and the take on screen re-shapes in well under a second (the keys' own samples follow a moment later), so PLAY, DRAG WAV, SAVE TAKE and the keys all carry the landscape. RANDOMIZE, SMOOTH, FREEZE (one moment for the whole take), EVOLVE (slow drift), A/B, NUMBERS, ANALYZER, RESET, and UNDO / REDO which are the plug-in's own (Cmd+Z undoes a landscape change like any other edit). The landscape is saved with each take in the session; takes with flat land, and every session saved before build 12, sound exactly as they did. Version 1.7.0. build 11: DRAG MIDI is one clean track again, the melody only (FL Studio reads it without asking), and a new DRAG CHORDS next to it drags the chords alone as their own one-track MIDI (the CHORD BED's notes when it is on, otherwise the take's chords; TEXTURE has none). VOICE all the way down now keeps the natural sound of your voice for any move you make on the roll, even past an octave (two or three octaves away), with no switch-over to another sound anywhere. SAVE TAKE also saves the chords MIDI beside the take. A tiny click that could happen at the start of some sung notes (with the VOICE knob up, mostly under a CHORD BED) is gone. Takes you made before keep sounding exactly as they did. Version 1.6.3. build 10: VOICE all the way down with MUSICAL on now keeps the natural sound of your voice for big jumps too (up to an octave), not just small ones, and the last little clicks it could leave are gone. DRAG MIDI now carries the chords as a second track (named CHORDS, channel 2): the CHORD BED's notes when it is on, otherwise the take's chords. Older takes you edit keep their own sound: the same syllables and, for CHOPS, the same chops in the same phrase. Version 1.6.2. build 9: VOICE all the way down with MUSICAL on now sounds much closer to your real recording: small re-pitches (up to a fifth) move your voice's own periods in order and keep its vowels exactly, instead of rebuilding it. A new CHORD BED slider on PLAY IT (INSTRUMENT) holds the take's chords softly under the melody on the same voice, so RICH chords and chord swaps can be heard (off by default). Older takes can be edited straight away (they upgrade themselves; undo brings the old one back). VARY remembers notes you deleted. A chop note you move to another octave really plays in that octave. TEXTURE edits re-render in a fraction of a second like the others. Version 1.6.1. build 8: UNDER THE HOOD's MELODY roll is yours to edit. Drag notes up and down (they only land on notes of the key, so nothing can go out of key) and left and right (onto the GRID: 1/4, 1/8, 1/16, 1/32), drag a note's right end to make it longer, double-click to add a note, double-click or DELETE to remove one, drag on empty space to select several, arrow keys move them, UNDO / REDO / RESET NOTES. The take re-renders in about half a second, your notes are saved with the session, VARY keeps them and DRAG MIDI exports them. A new PLAY IT tab has ArpEZator's controls: MASTER (simple to wild), CHORDS (AS WRITTEN / SIMPLE / RICH), the ARP (FIGURE, UP, DOWN, UP-DOWN, RANDOM, PENDULUM, CONVERGE, RATE 1/8 or 1/16, 1-3 OCTAVES) and the line between two notes (STEP, GLIDE, FATTEN). Click any chord name under the roll to swap it for another chord in the key; the melody follows. POP BRAIN and ACID BRAIN are now called LEARNED POP and LEARNED ACID. Version 1.6.0. build 7: a new style group, PARLOUR PIANO, with two moods - WISTFUL (an old-fashioned parlour piano: slow, gentle chords, a swaying left hand, a floating tune) and STILL NIGHT (slower and sparser, long held notes). It plays from a small model learned from 12 old piano scores; every take is new. Version 1.5.1. build 6: a much more beautiful sound. VOICE (the new knob next to TONE and SPACE for INSTRUMENT): all the way down plays your real recording, its actual words in the melody's timing; turn it up and the voice turns smoothly into a clean, soft instrument made from it (no buzz, no distortion). PAD gets DREAM (longer, glassier, dreamier, with a soft octave shimmer), TEXTURE gets DRIFT and CHOPS gets STUTTER. A STYLE browser with every melody style we have made (Block Step and Ghost House piano and synth styles, REVERIE, the learned POP and ACID brains, ArpEZator's arps, hooks, trap and hip hop) - click one to hear it - plus < > and LENGTH (1 to 16 bars). UNDER THE HOOD shows what each take type is doing, step by step, with its deeper knobs. VARY now makes a clear variation of the same idea. Version 1.5.0. build 5: the highlighted parts on the waveform are yours to edit, like slices in a sampler: drag a box to move it, drag its edges to resize it (they snap to zero crossings and to where syllables start; hold Shift to place freely), and the take rebuilds from your parts while the old one keeps playing. Double-click to add a part (a new chop), right-click for Delete / Split / Duplicate / Hear, Alt-drag copies, a click plays that part (and flashes its key for CHOPS), Cmd+Z undoes each edit. VARY keeps your parts, GENERATE starts fresh, and your parts are saved with the project. Version 1.4.0. build 4: a CLEAR switch (the small pill next to CHARACTER, on for new takes) that keeps your sound clean and true: a real sample on every key instead of one every few keys, a steady pitch with no wobble, chorus or detuned double, no warmth grit or limiter squash, cleaner PAD and TEXTURE grains over the voice itself, and CHOPS that play your original audio untouched when they are already in tune. Turn it off for the dreamier, blurrier sound; older projects open with it off so they sound the same. Version 1.3.0. build 3: the installer removes the old Ghost Slice the collection installer left in /Library (it was loading instead of the new one), version 1.2.0 so FL and Logic rescan. build 2: the new window exactly like the reference picture (deep indigo, violet -> cyan glow, Poppins font): glass panels, TAKE TYPE / CHARACTER tiles, waveform zoom + overview + TRIM + play the sound, take cards with mini waveforms, VELOCITY meter, SCALE box with key lock; INPUT moved into the gear menu
